      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where a template lives",
      "prov:value": "They moved there with the writer (bean `xsqm`, owner 2026-09-29: one copy of the README writers, in the tools repository): a template is part of the toolset, and somebody who wants different READMEs uses a different toolset over the same content.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean `xsqm`",
        "owner",
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/liquid-templates.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Versions are variables, never numbers",
      "prov:value": "- **README templates** get `release`: `version` (every instance declares one), and — for an instance declaring an `iriBase` — `major`, `agent` (for identifiers) and `human` (for pages), both `<iriBase>v<major>/` since the owner's 2026-10-23 ruling.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner's",
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/liquid-templates.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "An undefined variable is a message, not silence",
      "prov:value": "`docs/_plugins/liquid-undefined-warn.rb` does neither: every lookup runs as Liquid runs it, and at the end of the build each path that was ABSENT is printed as a warning with its count and pages, `site.data.*` first (owner, 2026-10-09, bean `8pyz`: *\"jekyll strict (if not error out, just message)\"*).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean `8pyz`",
        "owner",
        "2026-10-09"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    }
